      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c6c89e8d-6548-5f76-b648-0fef8c05e844",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Douglas\n- Songs: \"Man on the Edge\", \"Running Free\", \"Out of the Silent Planet\", \"Total Eclipse\", \"Mission From 'Arry\", \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be\", \"I Live My Way\", \"Run to the Hills\", \"2 Minutes to Midnight\", \"Be Quick or Be Dead\"\n- Albums: Best of the 'B' Sides, The Number of the Beast\n- Films: Falling Down\n- Topics: Iron Maiden singles and B-sides\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Douglas was born on September 25, 1944, and he is an American actor and producer.\n- \"Best of the 'B' Sides\" covers Iron Maiden singles from 1980's \"Running Free\" through 2000's \"Out of the Silent Planet\".\n- \"Total Eclipse\" was the B-side of \"Run to the Hills\" in 1982, and it was added to \"The Number of the Beast\" from 1998 onward.\n- \"Mission From 'Arry\" was the B-side of \"2 Minutes to Midnight\" in 1984.\n- \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be\" was the B-side of \"Be Quick or Be Dead\" in 1992.\n- \"I Live My Way\" was the B-side of \"Man on the Edge\" in 1995.\n- Several original Iron Maiden B-sides, including \"Total Eclipse,\" \"Mission From 'Arry,\" \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be,\" and \"I Live My Way,\" were excluded from \"Best of the 'B' Sides\".\n- The song \"Man on the Edge\" is based on the film \"Falling Down,\" which starred Michael Douglas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6293dc52-c112-5043-b5d0-c3fc1b45ba98",
        "text": "Page: Man on the Edge. Sentence: The song is based on the film \"Falling Down\", starring Michael Douglas.\nPage: Michael Douglas. Sentence: Michael Kirk Douglas (born September 25, 1944) is an American actor and producer.\nPage: Best of the 'B' Sides. Sentence: It covers all of their singles from their first (1980's \"Running Free\") to 2000's \"Out of the Silent Planet\", although several of the band's original B-sides were excluded from the collection: \"Total Eclipse\" (from \"Run to the Hills\", 1982, although this has been added to the album \"The Number of the Beast\" from 1998 onwards), \"Mission From 'Arry\" (from \"2 Minutes to Midnight\", 1984); \"Bayswater Ain't a Bad Place to Be\" (from \"Be Quick or Be Dead\", 1992); and \"I Live My Way\" (from \"Man on the Edge\", 1995).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
